    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28527" root="عر" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْرُورٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَارٌّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, applied to a
palm-tree (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَخْلَةٌ</span>), [and to land (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ</span>),] <i>Dunged
with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُرَّة</span> [q. v.]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And, without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, (assumed tropical:)  A
man <i>sullied,</i> or <i>bespattered, with evil;</i> or <i>aspersed:</i>
(S, Msb:) and <i>wronged,</i> or <i>treated unjustly</i> or
<i>injuriously; and reviled;</i> and <i>deprived of his
property.</i> (TA.)

